Package: grin
Title: Amortised Inference for General Recognition Theory
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Murray S.", "Bennett", email = "murray.bennett92@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Peter D.", "Kvam", role = "aut"),
    person("Joseph W.", "Houpt", role = "aut"))
Description: Amortised, uncertainty-calibrated inference of General Recognition
    Theory (GRT) perceptual representations from a 2x2 identification confusion
    matrix. A neural network, trained once on simulated data and shipped as a
    TorchScript graph, replaces per-participant maximum-likelihood fitting and
    returns a calibrated posterior over the 12 identified GRT parameters
    together with probabilities for perceptual independence and perceptual
    separability. Also provides a stopping-rule interface for adaptive designs
    and plotting functions for reporting results at the individual and group
    level. Inference runs natively through the 'torch' package and does not
    require Python. Companion to the 'grintools' package for Python; both wrap
    the same trained weights and are numerically verified to agree (see
    <https://github.com/MurraySBennett/grin>).
